s":5,"created_at":"2023-10-07T22:55:31Z","updated_at":"2024-05-07T21:34:33Z","closed_at":"2024-05-05T01:47:43Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nWhen building a python module with `pybind11` in `Debug` configuration, the wrong symbols are linked into the modules.\r\nThis bug occurs under the following conditions:\r\n - The python interpreter that is used for compilation/linkage does not have debug features (check via [this method](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/646518/python-how-to-detect-debug-interpreter))\r\n - The module is compiled using a `Debug` configuration\r\n - Now, when building the module the wrong symbols are used, since vcpkg always sets `Py_DEBUG` to true ([since this PR](https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/pull/31318))\r\n\r\n\r\n**Environment**\r\n- OS: Linux - Fedora 38\r\n- Compiler: gcc (GCC) 13.2.1 20230728 (Red Hat 13.2.1-1)\r\n- Python: Python 3.11.5 (Non Debug Build, important!)\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\nBuild a python module using pybind11 in debug configuration. The system python interpreter does not support any \r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nA python module build in `Debug`-Configuration and with a non-Debug System interpreter should work.\r\n\r\n**Failure logs**\r\nWhen importing the module the following errors get thrown by the python interpreter\r\n`ImportError: undefined symbol: _Py_RefTotal`\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nBy create a custom port of vcpkg without [this patch](https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/pull/31318) everything worked as expected. Maybe it would be a solution to only apply this patch on windows?\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"data-queue","id":144965964,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKQBTA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144965964?v=4"